\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Architectural comparison across four query-time table--text reasoning paradigms (offline GraphRAG frameworks like Microsoft GraphRAG and HippoRAG\nobreakspace  {}2 require corpus-wide pre-indexing and cannot ingest ad-hoc tables at query time). In contrast to unguided linear prompt concatenation\nobreakspace  {}(a), destructive question-driven graph pruning in ODYSSEY\nobreakspace  {}(b), and expensive multi-turn agentic loops in online GraphRAG systems like HydraRAG and ToG-3\nobreakspace  {}(c), the proposed QEG-RAG framework\nobreakspace  {}(d) dynamically instantiates a schema-preserving multigraph on-the-fly, retains complete evidence context, guides attention via deterministic multi-factor scored paths, and resolves bottlenecks via a bounded two-tier diagnostic-driven execution protocol.}}{4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:paradigms}{{1}{4}}
