\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Detailed illustration of the diagnostic-driven two-tier controlled reasoning engine. (Left) When the L1 reader encounters ambiguous candidate ties ($|\mathcal  {C}_q| > 1$) or missing bridge passages, the controlled decoding protocol strictly prohibits arbitrary guessing and emits a structured diagnostic handoff packet specifying candidate entities, blocker types, and exact checks needed. (Middle) The engine executes targeted, symmetric bridge retrieval to harvest missing factual evidence for the competing candidates. (Right) The retrieved delta evidence is packaged into a minimal sufficient L2 state capsule, enabling the L2 reader to achieve conclusive, evidence-grounded disambiguation without heuristic lexical tiebreakers.}}{9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:diagnostic-l2}{{3}{9}}
